{
  "note": "Hand-written. The phase 4 Done when (lifecycle 11.1): \"A resident charts a medical, wound and social visit as one encounter offline, saves and closes it, completes it later, and an attending attests it.\" One story for every test that runs it: apps/mobile/test/encounters/done_when_test.dart (steps 1 to 6, the phone's test server), live_encounters_test.dart (steps 1 to 7, the real API), apps/mobile/test/features/encounters/done_when_flow_test.dart (the screens), services/api/test/encounters-done-when.test.ts (steps 3, 5, 6 and 7 as raw changes and requests, and the shorter test) and the portal's half in apps/portal/e2e/attestation.spec.ts. The people are the seeded staff of db/seed/seed.ts, by email; a test that makes its own team makes them with these names, roles and credentials. Each note's answers are paths of its note type as released (packages/forms/generated/presets.json), the values the phone stores and sends; 'answers' are written at step 2, 'answersAtStep4' at step 4, and the note is finished with both. In 'steps', a string where a value is expected names each note's own value under that key ('answers', 'afterStep5', 'afterStep7'); a list of notes is in the visit's order, the order the phone made them in (the queue and the visit read keep it). A wound entry's ID and time ('edone001' and its entryAt) are the ones the domain layer's tests write through saveAnswer; the screens make their own. Everyone and everything here is invented.",

